Subject: [PATCH 06832/11362] wa30 L8: honest null with proven winning
 blueprint (no bank)

L8 ("final exam" -- two zones, both helper+thief mechanics, 13 blocks)
was not won this session: 3 episodes, 927/1000 budget, best state 11
of 13 blocks simultaneously placed with a 12th in transit at timer
expiry. Artifact reports it correctly -- max_level_reached stays 7,
level8_win_observed_live: false, action_sequence: [] (no candidate,
nothing to gate). No registry bump.

Logged the three mechanics discoveries as a dead_ends entry so a
future attempt starts from proven ground instead of re-deriving them:
(1) killing a laden thief is safe -- ACTION5 drops its cargo in place
rather than losing it; (2) thieves flee in open field and can only be
killed by camping their deterministic dump-patch tiles; (3) a zone
cannot stabilize while its thief lives, and the near-miss came from
killing both thieves too late in the timer, not from a flawed delivery
plan. A concrete tick-budgeted plan for the next attempt is preserved
in the artifact (south kill ~tick 24, north kill ~tick 45, then
unopposed ferrying to fungible bays, projected to finish by ~tick 115
against the ~125-action timer).

